ut equipment carries a two-hour limit.","short_summary":"A time-boxed social stop with billiards, board games, consoles and gaming PCs in one named room.","evidence_claim":"The official Games Room page lists billiards, board and card games, PlayStation 5, Nintendo Switch and gaming PCs, with equipment offered first-come, first-served for up to two hours.","source_url":"https://www.csun.edu/src/games-room","source_title":"Games Room","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Fall and spring hours are Monday–Friday, 10 a.m.–7 p.m.; the room is closed in summer. CSUN students may bring one guest, and patrons must sign in at the front desk.","cost_status":"unknown","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"csun-orange-grove-walk","subject_type":"sequence_stop","entity_name":"CSUN Orange Grove","title":"Friday: Cross the Orange Grove","subtitle":"Ease into campus through a five-acre landscape","notes":"Follow the decomposed-granite paths among the Valencia trees, keep fruit on the branches and use the walk to learn the campus’s northeast side.","short_summary":"A low-key outdoor transition through a surviving piece of the Valley’s agricultural landscape.","evidence_claim":"CSUN documents the Orange Grove as an approximately five-acre campus landscape with more than 400 Valencia orange trees and walkways that let visitors move among them.","source_url":"https://www.csun.edu/FPDC/about-our-campus","source_title":"About our Campus","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"The official page presents the grove as a place to visit, socialize and study but does not publish visitor hours; remain on established paths and observe campus postings.","cost_status":"unknown","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"csun-src-saturday","subject_type":"sequence_st