_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"The city lists Saturday hours of 8 a.m.–4 p.m. and Sunday as closed. Classes and reserved activities may require registration or fees; confirm open-use availability onsite.","cost_status":"unknown","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"csun-library-learning-commons","subject_type":"sequence_stop","entity_name":"University Library Learning Commons","title":"Saturday: Set Up Your Study Base","subtitle":"Learn where weekend academic work can happen","notes":"Enter on the main floor, locate technology help and study zones, then save the library hours page because semester and service-desk schedules differ.","short_summary":"A practical scouting stop for finding your future weekend study base before assignments begin.","evidence_claim":"The library states that its Learning Commons remains open whenever the University Library is open and provides technology-focused workshops and learning support.","source_url":"https://library.csun.edu/about/transformation/lc-faq","source_title":"Learning Commons FAQ","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Weekend hours vary by term and date. Consult the current calendar at https://library.csun.edu/hours before visiting; individual service desks may operate on shorter schedules.","cost_status":"unknown","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"museum-san-fernando-valley","subject_type":"sequence_stop","entity_name":"The Museum of the San Fernando Valley","title":"Saturday: Add Valley Context","subtitle":"Connect Northridge to its wider regional history","notes":"Head west on Nordhoff Street, allow time for the ongoing exhibits and ask a docent which display offers the clearest introduction to Valley history.","short_summary":"A nearby museum stop that frames the university within the history, arts and culture of the San Fernando Valley.","evidence_claim":"The museum’s official site identifies its Northridge location, advertises ongoing history and culture exhibits, and states that admission and parking are free.","source_url":"https://themuseumsfvnow.org/","source_title":"Explore the San Fernando Valley Museum Today","source_kind":"cultural_institution","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"The museum currently lists Saturday and Sunday hours of 11 a.m.–4 p.m. and Tuesday hours of 1–5 p.m. Verify the schedule before leaving campus.","cost_status":"free","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"two-up-two-down-sunset","subject_type":"sequence_stop","entity_name":"Two Up, Two Down","title":"Saturday: Watch a Kinetic Sculpture","subtitle":"Pause outside The Soraya near sunset","notes":"Stand back from the reflecting pool and watch how the stainless-steel blades respond to air and changing light; keep walkways clear for other visitors.","short_summary":"A brief golden-hour encounter with George Rickey’s moving stainless-steel public artwork.","evidence_claim":"CSUN identifies George Rickey’s kinetic sculpture “Two Up, Two Down” in front of The Soraya and specifically recommends seeing it in early morning or at sunset.","source_url":"https://newsroom.csun.edu/2023/08/17/safe-summer-sculpture-gallery-outdoors-explore-the-public-art-around-csuns-parklike-campus/","source_title":"Treasures on Campus: Explore the Public Art Around CSUN’s Parklike Campus","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":"2023-08-17","source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"The artwork is outdoors in front of The Soraya at campus-map coordinate E-1. The source calls the campus artworks enjoyable year-round but does not state formal access hours.","cost_status":"unknown","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"csun-sculpture-sunday","subject_type":"sequence_stop","entity_name":"CSUN Sculpture","title":"Sunday: Find the Letterform Sculpture","subtitle":"Begin with John T. Banks’s campus-scale sign","notes":"Approach from inside campus near Zelzah and Nordhoff, view the letterforms from several angles and stay separated from traffic at the campus edge.","short_summary":"A Sunday photo-and-design stop centered on a large sculptural rendering of the university initials.","evidence_claim":"CSUN’s public-art guide identifies John T. Banks’s “CSUN Sculpture” at the corner of Zelzah Avenue and Nordhoff Street, campus-map coordinate G-1.","source_url":"https://newsroom.csun.edu/2023/08/17/safe-summer-sculpture-gallery-outdoors-explore-the-public-art-around-csuns-parklike-campus/","source_title":"Treasures on Campus: Explore the Public Art Around CSUN’s Parklike Campus","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":"2023-08-17","source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"This is an outdoor campus artwork at coordinate G-1. The official guide describes the campus art as available to enjoy year-round but supplies no formal access hours.","cost_status":"unknown","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"csun-pond-finale","subject_type":"sequence_stop","entity_name":"CSUN Pond","title":"Sunday: Finish Beside the Pond","subtitle":"Close the loop where the grove and observatory meet","notes":"Use the bridge and established paths for one final campus pause; observe the pond and waterfall without feeding or disturbing resident wildlife.","short_summary":"A quiet final stop at the landscaped water feature embedded in the Orange Grove.","evidence_claim":"CSUN documents the pond in the Orange Grove as an enlarged water feature with a waterfall, meandering stream bed and bridge, relocated there during 2007–08.","source_url":"https://www.csun.edu/node/195321","source_title":"CSUN Orange Grove and Pond","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":n